Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:13:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1198/1252] HERESY 1168: the meter measures time: a word with
 no vowel and a stop closed against an affricate take a beat of their own; the
 tags list writes [END]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor 07.10.2026: «Допиши одиночные согласные доли, потому что мы не меряем по реальным слогам между 2 и 4 символами, а по
реальной затрате времени на произношение»; and to «подсказка вставляет [End]… Перевести вставку на [END]?»: «Да, измени».

In Russian, Ukrainian and Belarusian words: a word with no vowel (с, в, к, з, й, ў) and, inside a word, a stop right after a
vowel closed against an affricate (п|ц, т|ч, д|ц…; not сердце's silent д) are beats of their own. They count with the line's
syllables (the bar, its number and the group's ruler measure the whole), drawn lighter at the bar's end; under the box the
syllables stay syllables and the consonant beats are counted beside them. His line «Я же вижу глупцо́в с приду́рческим
планом» is 12 syllables and 2 beats: 14, his own split. The tags list inserts [END], as his songs write it (the cheat-sheet
keeps the official examples' [End]).

Kitchen suite: 393 passed, 0 failed, 7 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
